A||||4||MEC91Firebird||Easy Engine Removement?||||5||
Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||01-30-2001||12:24 AM||||I need to pull the engine(2.8 V6) out of an  86 SE. Any good guides on the internet?  any good advice, is it possible to do without a "Cherry Picker". Anything i should know? (beyond the manuals and the like)<BR>Thanks for the help!,<BR>Matt||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-30-2001||04:06 AM||||The whole engine cradle is held on with four bolts, and all the hoses and wires.  Unhook all that and pick up the body, then slide the engine/transaxle out from under.<P>The search function can bring up a thread somewhere with all the little details if needed.<BR>Details like where to hook and what to do with suspension and where wire bundle connections are and how to line it up to put back etc.<P><BR>                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||DJRice||01-30-2001||09:54 AM||||The haynes manual has a decent description of that procedure with pictures as well.  $12 at your local auto parts store.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000003||BN Boomer||01-30-2001||10:20 AM||||Well, saying that "four bolts, and all the hoses and wires" is a little bit simplistic. You've also got the brake calipers and struts to contend with. If you think that you may need to move the vehicle while the engine is out, dropping the cradle can make that quite difficult if not downright impossible. Dropping the cradle and handling the engine without a cherry picker is possible, but you'll still need some sort of chain host and something sturdy to attach it to or a damn strong back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Here's the V6 going back into my 85 GT...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/fiero1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Greg, aka Boomer<BR>Red 85 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.gmemd.com/locomotives/naf/images/sd70sm.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||CraZyRabBit||01-31-2001||08:07 AM||||It can be done very easily with two BIG floor jacks as you can see. Something overhead like a staircase and a whinch makes separation of the engine from the cradle child's play. The whinch cost me $15. <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierolift_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierolift3_2.jpg"> <P>Hope this helps,<BR>Mike.||||reg||14
